'''Kesmer Faloodi''' was a [[Reshtini]] nicknamed '''Bottomless''' because of his gluttonous appetite, though he did not know what his nickname referred to. Faloodi was a charming gossip who hoodwinked visitors to the [[Lomi Usqi Noodle Shop]] on the [[planet]] [[Ueda]] into covering his bills, and he could go [[Local day|days]] without paying for a meal.<ref name="Visual Guide" /> In [[132 BBY]],<ref name="Date">{{TheAcolyteDate}}</ref> Faloodi was sitting between<ref name="LF">{{Acolyte|Lost / Found}}</ref> the [[Wrosidian]]s [[Bihun]] and [[Basko]]<ref name="Visual Guide" /> while [[Diet|eating]] [[noodle]]s in the shop when the [[assassin]] [[Mae-ho Aniseya]] walked past them on her way to [[Indara's murder|kill]] [[Jedi Master]] [[Indara]]. As Aniseya walked by,<ref name="LF" /> the [[Service droid|server droid]] [[K7-1EG]] hovered beside Faloodi and used its [[processor]]s to calculate and recheck estimates for his appetite,<ref name="Visual Guide" /> while Faloodi gripped the sides of his bowl and slurped [[Foodstuff|noodles]] into his [[mouth]].<ref name="LF" /> [[Cabuck Junior]], the [[Gender|son]] of noodle shop owner [[Cabuck]],<ref name="Visual Guide" /> had a handmade toy of Faloodi.<ref name="Beccy Instagram">{{Instagram|username=youngsterbeccy|url=/p/C8r-IbKIyRH/?img_index=2|name=[[Beccy Henderson]]|date=2024-06-26|quote=Fun fact: The Bartenders child is holding a handmade teddy of the Noodle Slurper|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/tBVu5}}</ref> Faloodi wore a [[Color|red]] expanding [[Clothing|smock]] of stretch fabric. He had orange [[eye]]s, tan and blue skin, and a [[proboscis]].<ref name="Visual Guide" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|For a while, he became the mascot in our costume shop. Because he was a little guy, I wanted to give him a brighter color. The noodle shop is sort of smoky, and I just wanted to give him some personality and keep him simple.|Jennifer Bryan|<ref name="Art of Acolyte">''[[The Art of Star Wars: The Acolyte]]''</ref>}}
[[File:NoodleThief-ArtOfAcolyte.png|thumb|right|300px|Concept art by Barbra Araujo]]
Kesmer Faloodi first appeared in "[[Lost / Found]],"<ref name="LF" /> the first episode of the live-action [[Disney+]] series ''[[Star Wars: The Acolyte]]'', which aired on [[June 4]], [[2024]].<ref name="EPG">{{SW|url=series/the-acolyte/lost-found-episode-guide|text="Lost / Found" Episode Guide &#124; The Acolyte}}</ref> Prior to the release of the episode, he was first depicted in a trailer shown exclusively at [[Celebration Europe (2023)|Celebration Europe]]<ref name="Celebration">{{CelebrationTrailer|''[[Star Wars: The Acolyte]]''|Celebration Europe (2023)}}</ref> during the [[Lucasfilm]] Studio Showcase on [[April 7]], [[2023]].<ref name="Studio Showcase">{{SW|url=news/swce-2023-lucasfilm-studio-showcase|text=SWCE 2023: 11 Highlights from Lucasfilm's Studio Showcase}}</ref> He was first identified in [[Pablo Hidalgo]]'s [[2025]] reference book, ''[[Star Wars: The Acolyte: The Visual Guide]]''.<ref name="Visual Guide" /> [[Claire Roi Harvey]], [[Lynn Robertson Bruce]], [[Adrian Parish]], and [[Beccy Henderson]] puppeteered Faloodi, and [[Nicolas Ferrard]] wrangled his noodles.<ref name="Instagram">{{Instagram|username=claireroiharvey|url=/p/C5SfVl_oMYu/?hl=en|name=[[Claire Roi Harvey]]|date=2024-04-03|quote=REPOST from @youngsterbeccy: Made the Star Wars trailer 🥹🍜👽 I’m puppeteering the noodle slurping alien in the middle with @claireroiharvey @lynnrb3 & @adyfparish (& @obviouslycookies wrangling noodles)|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/zb1Gu}}</ref> [[Tim Berry]] designed the puppet's body and part of its animatronic head, which was then finished by Adrian Parish. Faloodi was designed and sculpted by [[Stefano Cordioli]].<ref name="Cordiolo Instagram">{{Instagram|username=stef_cordioli|url=/p/C8jsrP1Kmzy/|name=[[Stefano Cordioli]]|date=2024-06-23|quote=" The noodles  slurper"  was  one of the characters  I  designed and sculpted for Neal Scanlan for 1st episode of #theacolyte. The animatronic head and the puppet  body was designed by @timatronics and then  finished  by Ady Parish. Puppeteered by @claireroiharvey @youngsterbeccy Lynn Robertson Bruce and @adyfparish|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/2esjE}}</ref>

Concept art of Faloodi was created by [[Andre Gilbert]] and [[Barbra Araujo]]. Because of Faloodi's small size and the smokiness of the noodle shop, costume designer [[Jennifer Bryan]] wanted to give him a brighter color to give him personality and also keep him simple. According to Bryan, Faloodi became the mascot of the costume shop. Creature effects supervisor [[Neal Scanlan]] compared Faloodi to "your dog" because he ate other's meals and passed on gossip.<ref name="Art of Acolyte" /> The scenes in the Lomi Usqi Noodle Shop were filmed at [[Shinfield Studios]],<ref name="Fantha Part I">{{WebCite|url=https://www.fanthatracks.com/news/the-acolyte-a-journey-to-the-filming-locations-part-1-madeira|text=The Acolyte: A journey to the filming locations Part 1: Madeira|archivedate=20241204220147}}</ref> [[Wikipedia:England|England]].<ref name="Julian Foddy">{{Lucasfilm|url=news/julian-foddy-acolyte|text=''The Acolyte'' Visual Effects Supervisor Julian Foddy}}</ref>

